@page "/severity"

<PageTitle>Severity levels</PageTitle>
<h1>Severity levels</h1>
<p>Warnings and infos render distinctly and never block submission; only errors do.</p>

<TeachingPanel CodeFiles="@(new[] { "Listing.cs", "SeverityLevels.razor", "SeverityLevels.razor.cs" })">
    <Rules>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Title</strong> — required (error severity: blocks submission).</li>
            <li><strong>Description</strong> — an exclamation mark draws a <em>warning</em> (advisory: never blocks).</li>
            <li><strong>Tags</strong> — more than five draws an <em>info</em> (advisory: never blocks). Advisories validate live, when you leave the field.</li>
            <li>A live pass only records a verdict for the field(s) that triggered it, even though validating any one field runs the whole model to get there. Title starts required and empty but untouched: no live pass has ever recorded anything for it, so its error stays invisible until a submit checks every field at once.</li>
            <li>Advisory-only submissions still announce the summary — screen readers hear the warnings and infos that did not block.</li>
            <li>This page renders <strong>two</strong> summaries rather than one: <code>Show="SummaryFilter.Errors"</code> lists only what blocks, and <code>Show="SummaryFilter.Advisories"</code> lists the warnings and infos that do not. A summary with nothing to show renders nothing at all.</li>
            <li>Two summaries mean two announcements, and an issue listed by both would be read twice — which is why these two filters are chosen to be disjoint rather than one of them being left unfiltered.</li>
        </ul>
    </Rules>
    <TryIt>
        <ol>
            <li>Type <code>Great synth!</code> into Description and leave the field — the warning appears immediately, in amber.</li>
            <li>Enter six comma-separated tags and leave the field — the info appears, in purple-blue.</li>
            <li>With a warning and an info showing and Title still empty and untouched, look at the two summary blocks — the advisory summary is populated and the error summary is absent, not because Title is valid but because no live pass has ever recorded a verdict for it; only a submit will.</li>
            <li>Fill Title and submit — it goes through: the status line counts the warnings and infos that did NOT block.</li>
            <li>Clear Title and submit — only the error blocks; the advisories keep their place and colour in the summary.</li>
        </ol>
    </TryIt>
</TeachingPanel>

<FormidableForm @ref="_form" Model="_listing">
    <FormidableSummary Show="SummaryFilter.Errors" ErrorsHeading="Errors" />
    <FormidableSummary Show="SummaryFilter.Advisories" WarningsHeading="Warnings" InfosHeading="Infos" />

    <div class="field"><label>Title <FormidableInputText @bind-Value="_listing.Title" /></label>
        <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _listing.Title" /></div>
    <div class="field"><label>Description <FormidableInputText @bind-Value="_listing.Description" /></label>
        <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _listing.Description" /></div>
    <div class="field"><label>Tags (comma-separated) <FormidableInputText @bind-Value="_listing.Tags" /></label>
        <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _listing.Tags" /></div>

    <div class="actions"><button type="button" class="primary" @onclick="Submit">Submit</button></div>
</FormidableForm>

<p role="status">@_status</p>
